.TH "Z" "1" "September 2026" "" ""
.
.SH "NAME"
\fBz\fR \- jump around
.
.SH "Name"
z \- jump around: port of rupa\'s z
.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBz [\-cdehlprtyx] string1 string2\.\.\.\fR
.
.br
\fBzo [\-cdehlprtyx] string1 string2\.\.\.\fR
.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Port of rupa\'s z:
.
.P
Tracks your most used directories, based on \'frecency\'\. The data is stored in a file located at \fB$Z_DATA\fR\.
.
.P
After a short learning phase, z will take you to the most \'frecent\' directory that matches ALL of the strings given on the command line, in order\.
.
.P
For more details about frecency, see https://github\.com/rupa/z\.
.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-clean\fR
Removes directories that no longer exist from \fB$Z_DATA\fR\.
.
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-echo\fR
Prints the best match\. No cd\.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-directory\fR
Opens the best match with the configured file manager\. No cd\.
.
.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show a brief help message\.
.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print the installed version string without changing directory\.
.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-list\fR
Show a list of matches and their scores\. No cd\.
.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-rank\fR
Match by rank only\.
.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-recent\fR
Match by recent only\.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-fuzzy\fR
Enables fuzzy fallback matching for this search\. Exact and case\-insensitive matches take priority\.
.TP
\fB\-\-increase [N]\fR
Increases the current directory's ranking score by N (default 10) without changing directory\.
.TP
\fB\-\-decrease [N]\fR
Decreases the current directory's ranking score by N (default 15) without changing directory\.
.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-purge\fR
Deletes all entries from \fB$Z_DATA\fR\.
.
.
.TP
\fB\-x\fR, \fB\-\-delete\fR
Removes the current directory from \fB$Z_DATA\fR\.
.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.
.TP
\fBz foo\fR
Goes to directory best matching \fBfoo\fR\.
.
.TP
\fBzo foo\fR
Opens file manager of directory best matching \fBfoo\fR\.
.
.TP
\fBz \-t foo\fR
Goes to most recent directory matching \fBfoo\fR\.
.
.TP
\fBz \-x\fR
Removes the current directory from \fB$Z_DATA\fR\.
.TP
\fBz \-\-increase 20\fR
Boosts the current directory's ranking score by 20\.
.
.TP
\fBz \-\-decrease 10\fR
Lowers the current directory's ranking score by 10\.
.
.
.SH "CONFIGURATION"
.
.TP
\fBset \-U Z_CMD "j"\fR
Change commands to \fBj\fR and \fBjo\fR
.
.TP
\fBset \-U Z_DATA "$HOME/\.foo"\fR
Set data file to \fB$HOME/\.foo\fR
.
.TP
\fBset \-U Z_FUZZY true\fR
Enables fuzzy fallback matching for searches\.
.TP
\fBset \-U ZO_METHOD "opencmd"\fR
Runs \fBopencmd dir\fR on \fBzo dir\fR (defaults to \fBopen\fR or \fBxdg\-open\fR)
.
.TP
\fBset \-U Z_OWNER "username"\fR
Ensure data file is owned by \fBusername\fR\. This prevents usage of \fBz\fR with \fBsudo\fR to cause file to be inaccessible in non\-sudo sessions\.
.P
The data file stores an escaped path field so special characters remain lossless\. Existing records remain readable and migrate during updates or cleanup\. The file uses private permissions, and rewrites preserve the configured owner\.
.

